<title>USA: CBS to pay $100 mln for stake in Sportsline - NYT.</title>
<headline>CBS to pay $100 mln for stake in Sportsline - NYT.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Westinghouse's CBS network plans to invest $100 million to buy a one-third stake in Sportsline USA Inc, an on-line sports service based in Ft. Lauderdale, Florida, the New York Times said Tuesday.</p>
<p>The report, citing people familiar with the talks, said CBS plans to make the announcement today at a news conference.</p>
<p>CBS' move comes amid negotiations by Walt Disney, the owner of ABC, for a stake in Starwave Corp, which runs the ESPNet SportsZone, a joint venture between Disney and Starwave that is considered one of the most commercially successful sites on the Internet.</p>
<p>((-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
